WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.889
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The I-Statement Builder.

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:19.779
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:23.313
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:26.846
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:26.846 --> 00:00:35.091
Sometimes something happens with a friend, and the words inside you feel hot and tangled.

00:00:35.091 --> 00:00:44.514
Hot words can land like blame: "You always—" "You never—" Blame makes ears close. The truth stops getting through.

00:00:44.514 --> 00:00:55.115
There is a way to say the same truth so ears stay open. It is a sentence built from three pieces, and it starts with "I."

00:00:55.115 --> 00:00:59.827
Let me show you how to build it.

00:00:59.827 --> 00:01:10.428
Piece one: "I feel…" and name the feeling. "I feel sad." "I feel frustrated." The feeling is yours, so it starts with you.

00:01:10.428 --> 00:01:21.029
Piece two: "…when…" and say what happened — just the plain event. "…when my tower fell." Not what kind of person they are. Just what happened.

00:01:21.029 --> 00:01:31.630
Piece three: "I need…" and say what would help. "I need a turn to build it again." A need is a door the other person can actually walk through.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:41.053
Put together, it sounds like this: "I feel sad when my tower fell. I need a turn to build it again."

00:01:41.053 --> 00:01:42.231
One more, a gentle one: "I feel left out when the game starts without me. I need someone to call my name."

00:01:42.231 --> 00:01:52.832
Watch out for the disguise: "I feel that you…" is blame wearing the sentence's clothes. If "you" does the action in your feeling piece, rebuild it.

00:01:52.832 --> 00:02:03.433
And hear this clearly: an I-statement is an offer, not a lever. It tells your truth. It does not force the other person to agree, or to say yes.

00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:11.678
They might say yes. They might not be ready. Both are allowed. You said the truth kindly, and that part is already done.

00:02:11.678 --> 00:02:12.856
We practice with made-up stories here — never with a real name, never with a real moment from our room. Practice stays kind.

00:02:12.856 --> 00:02:21.101
I feel. When. I need.

00:02:21.101 --> 00:02:26.990
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.702
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:31.702 --> 00:02:37.591
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:37.591 --> 00:02:43.481
You're ready for what's next.
